Relevant tables / columns and how they could be used  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "path": to keep only *.py / *.r source files  
  – "id": to join with SAMPLE_CONTENTS so that we can read the file body  
  – "repo_name", "ref": optional grouping / filtering if required  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "id": joins back to SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "content": whole file text in which we will search for  
      • Python import / from‑import statements  
      • R  library(…) / require(…) calls  
  – "sample_path", "sample_repo_name": same information as in SAMPLE_FILES, can be used instead of a join when convenient  

Typical conditions we will need  
– WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py'  (Python files)  
– WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.r'   (R files)  
– REGEXP_LIKE("content", …)  to capture module / package names  
– GROUP BY "module"  
– ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC  
– LIMIT 5  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all different, each limited to 20 rows).  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes, comments start with -- .  

```sql
-- 1) Description: show a quick sample of Python file paths that exist in the snapshot
SELECT "repo_name", "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: show a quick sample of R script paths
SELECT "repo_name", "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.r'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: count total *.py files in the snapshot
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "python_file_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py';
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: count total *.r files in the snapshot
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "r_file_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.r';
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: pull one random Python file together with its full text content
SELECT f."repo_name",
       f."path",
       c."content"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: list the first import / from‑import module that REGEXP_SUBSTR finds in each Python file
SELECT f."path",
       REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                     '\\b(import|from)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                     1, 1, 'e', 2)      AS "first_module"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: preview the most common Python modules (very rough, first occurrence only)
SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                     '\\b(import|from)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                     1, 1, 'e', 2)      AS "module_name",
       COUNT(*)                         AS "cnt"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY 2 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: extract R package names referenced by library() or require()
SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                     '\\b(library|require)\\s*\\(\\s*["'']?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                     1, 1, 'e', 2)      AS "package",
       COUNT(*)                         AS "cnt"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.r'
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY 2 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: union Python modules and R packages into one list, keep the origin flag
SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                     '\\b(import|from)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                     1, 1, 'e', 2)      AS "module",
       'python'                         AS "lang"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.py'

UNION ALL

SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                     '\\b(library|require)\\s*\\(\\s*["'']?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                     1, 1, 'e', 2)      AS "module",
       'r'                              AS "lang"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
       ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.r'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: final query – top 5 most frequent modules/packages across Python & R scripts
SELECT "module", COUNT(*) AS "frequency"
FROM  (
        /* --- Python modules --- */
        SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                             '\\b(import|from)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                             1, 1, 'e', 2) AS "module"
        FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
        JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
               ON c."id" = f."id"
        WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.py'

        UNION ALL

        /* --- R packages --- */
        SELECT REGEXP_SUBSTR(c."content",
                             '\\b(library|require)\\s*\\(\\s*["'']?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)',
                             1, 1, 'e', 2) AS "module"
        FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"   f
        JOIN   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
               ON c."id" = f."id"
        WHERE  f."path" ILIKE '%.r'
      ) t
WHERE "module" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "module"
ORDER BY "frequency" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```
